          }
        ]
      },
      "description": "This course introduces the numerical solution of systems of linear equations and optimization problems, as related to computational mathematics and data science. Topics include matrix factorizations LU, LDLT, Cholesky, QR, and SVD factorization, iterative methods including Jacobi, Gauss-Seidel, SOR, and conjugate gradient, eigenvalue and singular value problems, and introduction to gradient-based unconstrained optimization methods.",
